  "host": "Published @deepseek-ai/dsh 0.2.0-rc.1 installed with npm into an isolated prefix; a fresh DSH home, user home and pnpm store for every capture; no Host source modifications",
  "mnemonCliVersion": "0.2.7",
  "pnpmVersion": "11.19.0",
  "model": "DeepSeek API, deepseek-flash (shown as DeepSeek-V41-Flash)",
  "browser": "Headless Google Chrome driven over the DevTools protocol",
  "packages": "The 18 packages `pnpm release:version` produces from this revision (dsh-mnemon 0.5.19 and its pinned plugins), served before they were on npm by a local registry that adds them to npm's real metadata as the newest release; the Add plugin dialog showed the install source DSH chose (Chinese: its speed check picked the mainland China mirror; English: npm's own registry, the choice a user outside mainland China gets), and a small pnpm wrapper sent that source's requests to the local registry. The refused-install screens used npm's real metadata only.",
  "starterOffScreens": "Captured 2026-09-29 02:22 (Asia/Shanghai) on the same published DSH 0.2.0-rc.1 with npm's published dsh-mnemon 0.5.19, installed with `dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-mnemon@0.5.19` into a fresh DSH home, after the `mnemon-starter` row was turned off in the profile patch (`disabled: true`, as the Plugins page stores it). DSH started with the warning `mnemon-bundle (cordis:group): pending (waiting for service: mnemonStarterReady)` and no Memory System; turning the switch back on brought the Memory System up without a restart, on DSH 0.1.7-rc.2 as well.",
  "conversation": "The first message is typed; the live model decides to write runtime memory, and the reply and entries are the model's own. Another run words them differently.",
  "recordingNote": "Chrome screencast frames played at their own timestamps (H.264 CRF 27, 30 fps, no audio; GIF 880 px, 8 fps). The install wait plays 4x and the reply wait 4x, with an on-screen badge; pauses while screenshots were taken are left out. A drawn cursor ring shows where each click lands.",
  "data": {
    "personalData": false,
    "credentials": false,
    "apiKey": "passed to DSH through the environment for the live conversation; never typed or shown"
  },
